  "body": "## Description\r\n\r\n- Merged the `counts` and `probability` log variables into `measurement_outcomes` \r\n- Added a new function into utilities: `qaoa_wavefunction`. (Similar in logic with `qaoa_proabilities` but outputs the wavefunction instead)\r\n- `measurement_outcomes` is now assigned when `wavefunction`, `expectation`,  `expectation_w_uncertainity` or `get_counts` methods are called for the respective backends.\r\n- Updated unittests for the new changes\r\n- Added unittests that checks the results returned by all the simulator backends are consistent. (i.e. if `optimization_progress` is requested, the `intermediate measurement outcomes` are returned.) (#35)\r\n- Merged changes from `dev` into this branch\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n[//]: <> (- [ ] My code follows the style guidelines of this project)\r\n\r\n- [x] I have performed a self-review of my code.\r\n- [ ] I have commented my code and used numpy-style docstrings\r\n- [ ] I have made corresponding updates to the documentation.\r\n- [x] My changes generate no new warnings\r\n- [x] I have added/updated tests to make sure bugfix/feature works.\r\n- [x] New and existing unit tests pass locally with my changes.\r\n\r\n[//]: <> (- [ ] Any dependent changes have been merged and published in downstream modules)\r\n\r\n## Type of change\r\n\r\nPlease delete options that are not relevant.\r\n\r\n- [x] Bug fix (non-breaking change which fixes an issue)\r\n- [x] New feature (non-breaking change which adds functionality)\r\n- [x] Breaking change (fix or feature that would cause existing functionality to not work as expected)\r\n- [x] This change requires a documentation update\r\n\r\n## How Has This Been Tested?\r\n\r\ntest_all.py",
